            <profile id="8857-f596-3385-6797" name="Equipment and options (as printed in WAB2 army list)" publicationId="0641-2ee1-c462-c414" hidden="false" typeId="b19e-ee0c-17d1-6e33" typeName="Equipment and Notes">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Text" typeId="63ac-8f60-d28a-2232">Sword. May have light armour +3 pts, heavy armour +4 pts, shield +1 pt, large shield +2 pts. May have thrusting spear free. May ride a horse (free), his movement is increased to 6, and gains +1 save. May not have a shield if mounted. Polemarch: if present, Greek mercenary troops may make Leadership tests using their paymaster's Army General, and gain all benefits of the Army Battle Standard; if killed, all Greek mercenaries must pass a Panic test (ignored if the Army General is killed). 0-1. (Alexander the Great p.79)</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
            <profile id="f8d4-5e99-08b3-fc16" name="Armour Save" hidden="false" typeId="0dbe-f4ed-ef08-8e86" typeName="Armour Save">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Save" typeId="603e-2898-6af9-6cf1">None</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="With conditional bonuses" typeId="5882-dd5a-bc28-4024">-</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="Notes" typeId="d5e4-804e-6192-0114">Armour save from armour, shield and barding bonus pips (rulebook pp.95-98); maximum 3+ (2+ for barded cavalry). M already includes encumbrance for armour/barding (p.96). Conditional pips are in the next column.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
