            <cost name="pts" typeId="points" value="10"/>
          </costs>
        </selectionEntry>
      </selectionEntries>
    </selectionEntry>
  </selectionEntries>
  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="49d5-6483-362e-2cbe" name="Greek Mercenaries (Alexander the Great) - List Notes" publicationId="0641-2ee1-c462-c414" hidden="false">
      <description>GREEK MERCENARIES 404-301 BC (Alexander the Great, pp.79-80). These troops are offered as Mercenaries to be used with the armies in the book, not as a stand-alone army list - although it could be used with an opponent's consent (Xenophon's Ten Thousand). The book gives no percentage limits.
Oracles: Greek Mercenaries taken by an army that uses oracles may use the army's pool of oracles; if hired by an army that does not use oracles, no oracles may be used. Unit selection: Greek Mercenaries may not have unit standards. The minimum size for a regiment is five models, there is no upper limit. One model in each unit may be upgraded to a Leader (+5 pts) or a Musician (+5 pts). Not enforced: one Greek Horse unit per Hoplite or Peltast unit (entered as a 0-1 unit); one mercenary character per Hoplite, Cavalry or Peltast unit; every second Psiloi unit with bows or slings.

ARMY COMPOSITION:
[Greek Mercenaries]
  GREEK MERCENARIES 404-301 BC (Alexander the Great, pp.79-80). These troops are offered as Mercenaries to be used with the armies in the book, not as a stand-alone army list - although it could be used with an opponent's consent (Xenophon's Ten Thousand). The book gives no percentage limits.
Oracles: Greek Mercenaries taken by an army that uses oracles may use the army's pool of oracles; if hired by an army that does not use oracles, no oracles may be used. Unit selection: Greek Mercenaries may not have unit standards. The minimum size for a regiment is five models, there is no upper limit. One model in each unit may be upgraded to a Leader (+5 pts) or a Musician (+5 pts). Not enforced: one Greek Horse unit per Hoplite or Peltast unit (entered as a 0-1 unit); one mercenary character per Hoplite, Cavalry or Peltast unit; every second Psiloi unit with bows or slings.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
